title: "Step 4 · Report"
description: Read and export the reports of the period, including the F5 report.
sidebar:
  order: 13
---

Step 4 holds the reports of the period. Each report can be exported to Excel.

| Report | What it shows |
|---|---|
| **Management Accounts** | The management accounts for the period. |
| **F5 report** | The one-page GST F5 form from the confirmed figures, with the worksheet and the tax detail as separate attachments. |
| **Trial Balance** | Every account's balance. An account whose balance is on the unexpected side is marked **Abnormal balance**. |
| **Control Accounts** | The receivables, payables and other control accounts agreed to their detail. |
| **General Ledger** | Every entry, account by account. |
| **Balance Sheet** / **Profit and Loss** | The financial position and the result for the period. |
| **A/R Aging Detail** / **A/P Aging Detail** | Receivables and payables by age. |

{% screenshot id="bookkeeping/report-trial-balance" caption="The trial balance of ABC PTE. LTD., 30 September 2026." /%}

## F5 report

The F5 report is generated from the figures confirmed under **Review › F5 check**, so it always matches what was confirmed. If the figures have not been confirmed, the page shows a draft marked DRAFT and asks for the figures to be confirmed first.

{% steps %}

1. Under **Review › F5 check**, a manager selects **Generate F5**. This confirms the figures.
2. Give the F5 report to the client to approve.
3. After the return is filed in myTax, go back to **Review › F5 check**, enter the IRAS acknowledgement number and select **Mark as filed**.

{% /steps %}

To change confirmed figures before filing, a manager selects **Withdraw the F5 confirmation** on **Review › F5 check**, the books are corrected and the F5 is generated again. A filed return cannot be withdrawn, and a quarter marked as filed cannot be reopened: if the books change after filing, the difference is reported in a later return.

{% aside type="note" %}
Operon does not file the F5 with IRAS. Filing is done by the firm, after the client approves the return.
{% /aside %}
